PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported)
  Modal(size=sm)          → sheet content in a NavigationStack (focus trap + dismiss for free), title
                            `${def.name} Settings` via "%@ Settings", toolbar `.cancellationAction` Cancel.
  FormSection             → titled section header (Font.TS.bodySm semibold, textSecondary, isHeader).
  Select                  → native menu `Picker` styled with the design tokens (the same primitive
                            `TSSelect` wraps). Labels resolve through the surface i18n TABLE and render
                            verbatim — `TSSelect`'s LocalizedStringKey would route to the main catalog,
                            so the surface uses the underlying primitive + the P1/S10 facade, matching the
                            AdvancedSettings / WebhookChannelsSection precedent.
  Toggle                  → native `Toggle(.switch)` tinted accent, surface-table label.
  Button (Cancel/Save)    → `TSButton` (.ghost / .primary) with surface-table `Text` labels.
  i18n                    : every web key (dashboard.settings.* + common.cancel/save) + the native envelope
                            keys present in WidgetSettingsModal.strings; ZERO English literals in the Swift.
  a11y                    : every control has a VoiceOver label; the vehicle section exposes a per-phase
                            spoken summary; the freshness chip / banner / retry are labelled; Dynamic Type
                            via Font.TS; Reduce-Motion safe (no bespoke animation).
  telemetry (P1/S11)      : `view.opened` surface="WidgetSettingsModal" emitted once on appear via the
                            WidgetSettingsTelemetry seam (default OSLog sink, redaction-safe).

STATES (every state renders — never a blank section; scoped to the useVehicles binding)
  loading  → "Loading vehicles…" note beneath a usable selector (All Vehicles option present).
  ready    → populated selector.
  empty    → "No vehicles found — showing All Vehicles." (selector keeps the 'all' option).
  error    → inline "Couldn't load vehicles" + Retry affordance (selector still usable).
  stale    → Stale freshness chip + "Reconnecting…" banner + one guarded auto-refresh.
  offline  → Offline chip + "Offline — showing the last synced vehicles" banner, cached options kept.

